WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.582
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:05.882 --> 00:00:09.396
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:16.528
Unit fourteen: Word Formation: Prefixes and Suffixes. Today you will build new words from base words.

4
00:00:16.828 --> 00:00:19.643
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.972
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:25.783
Prefix.

7
00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:29.677
Prefix means letters added to the front of a word.

8
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:31.575
Un- is a prefix.

9
00:00:32.183 --> 00:00:35.103
Your turn. Say: Prefix.

10
00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:38.979
Prefix.

11
00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:40.625
Suffix.

12
00:00:41.617 --> 00:00:44.290
Suffix means letters added to the end of a word.

13
00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:46.349
-ness is a suffix.

14
00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.626
Your turn. Say: Suffix.

15
00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:53.619
Suffix.

16
00:00:54.383 --> 00:00:55.257
Opposite.

17
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.760
Opposite means a word with the reverse meaning.

18
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.605
Happy and unhappy are opposites.

19
00:01:02.217 --> 00:01:04.439
Your turn. Say: Opposite.

20
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.127
Opposite.

21
00:01:08.883 --> 00:01:09.606
Noun.

22
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:13.650
Noun means a word for a person, place or thing.

23
00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.681
Happiness is a noun.

24
00:01:16.283 --> 00:01:18.727
Your turn. Say: Noun.

25
00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:22.428
Noun.

26
00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:24.277
Adjective.

27
00:01:25.283 --> 00:01:27.736
Adjective means a word that describes.

28
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.862
Happy is an adjective.

29
00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:33.300
Your turn. Say: Adjective.

30
00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:37.111
Adjective.

31
00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:38.805
Adverb.

32
00:01:39.817 --> 00:01:42.408
Adverb means a word that describes a verb.

33
00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:44.738
Happily is an adverb.

34
00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:48.200
Your turn. Say: Adverb.

35
00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:52.011
Adverb.

36
00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:53.693
Base word.

37
00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:57.728
Base word means the main word before adding parts.

38
00:01:58.317 --> 00:01:59.898
Happy is the base word.

39
00:02:00.483 --> 00:02:03.020
Your turn. Say: Base word.

40
00:02:05.867 --> 00:02:06.868
Base word.

41
00:02:07.617 --> 00:02:09.129
Family of words.

42
00:02:10.117 --> 00:02:12.557
Family of words means words from the same root.

43
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.022
Care, careful and careless.

44
00:02:15.617 --> 00:02:18.385
Your turn. Say: Family of words.

45
00:02:21.233 --> 00:02:22.501
Family of words.

46
00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.951
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.817 --> 00:02:31.128
Visal, how do prefixes and suffixes change words?

48
00:02:32.217 --> 00:02:45.132
A prefix changes the meaning, for example un-, in-, dis- and im- make opposites: unhappy, incorrect, dislike and impossible. A suffix changes the word class.

49
00:02:46.217 --> 00:02:47.798
Which suffixes should I know?

50
00:02:48.883 --> 00:03:03.798
For nouns: -ness, -tion, -ment and -er, such as kindness and teacher. For adjectives: -ful, -less and -able. For adverbs: -ly, such as quickly.

51
00:03:04.883 --> 00:03:06.558
How do I use them in a test?

52
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:18.803
Look at the gap. Decide if it needs a noun, adjective or adverb. Then choose the form of the base word that fits, and check whether it should be negative.

53
00:03:19.967 --> 00:03:21.827
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:22.683 --> 00:03:27.214
Grammar focus: Base word plus prefix and suffix.

55
00:03:27.514 --> 00:03:28.724
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:31.776
She is unhappy because she lost her bag.

57
00:03:32.683 --> 00:03:34.648
He answered quickly and correctly.

58
00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:43.361
Decide if the gap needs a noun, adjective or adverb, then add the right suffix or prefix. Check the spelling of the new word.

59
00:03:44.117 --> 00:03:47.663
Be careful! Don't say: He is unhelpfully.

60
00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.809
Say: He is unhelpful.

61
00:03:52.109 --> 00:03:53.713
Check the word class.

62
00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.419
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:58.233 --> 00:03:59.583
Changing Words.

64
00:03:59.883 --> 00:04:03.113
Sophea reads a sentence with a gap before the word help.

65
00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.761
The gap needs an adjective that means 'giving help'.

66
00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:09.604
She adds -ful to make helpful.

67
00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.761
In another sentence she needs an adverb from careful.

68
00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:17.080
She writes carefully and checks the spelling.

69
00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:22.134
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:22.983 --> 00:04:24.878
The opposite of happy is blank.

71
00:04:25.178 --> 00:04:28.762
A, inhappy. B, dishappy. C, unhappy.

72
00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.230
The answer is C: unhappy.

73
00:04:35.383 --> 00:04:37.000
The noun from kind is blank.

74
00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.988
A, kindness. B, kindly. C, kinder.

75
00:04:44.533 --> 00:04:46.382
The answer is A: kindness.

76
00:04:47.517 --> 00:04:49.412
An adverb from quick is blank.

77
00:04:49.712 --> 00:04:53.133
A, quicker. B, quickly. C, quickness.

78
00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.306
The answer is B: quickly.

79
00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:01.287
The suffix -ful makes blank.

80
00:05:01.587 --> 00:05:05.182
A, verbs. B, numbers. C, adjectives.

81
00:05:08.733 --> 00:05:11.139
The answer is C: adjectives.

82
00:05:12.283 --> 00:05:13.877
What does Sophea make from help?

83
00:05:14.177 --> 00:05:18.828
A, helpful. B, helpness. C, helpless only.

84
00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:24.134
The answer is A: helpful.

85
00:05:25.333 --> 00:05:28.415
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:32.283
How do you use prefixes and suffixes in an exam?

87
00:05:41.083 --> 00:05:42.584
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:42.884 --> 00:05:55.964
I look at the gap and decide which word class it needs. Then I add a prefix or suffix to the base word, and I check the spelling. If the meaning is negative, I choose a prefix like un- or im-.

89
00:05:56.264 --> 00:05:58.078
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:58.983 --> 00:06:04.480
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and base word plus prefix and suffix.

91
00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:09.998
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

92
00:06:10.298 --> 00:06:13.171
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:13.471 --> 00:06:17.412
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

